  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "5FeTOMxVx5NOJ5JGTT0Rsik9Hjk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:01.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "A freshly built reactor does not sync. The sync subsystem in `@powerhousedao/reactor` is opt-in, and there are exactly two ways to opt in on the `ReactorBuilder`: `withChannelScheme(scheme)` or `withSync(syncBuilder)`. Call neither and `module.syncModule` is `undefined` \u2014 the reactor stores and reduces operations locally and never contacts a remote.\n\n`withChannelScheme` is the shortcut. It constructs the channel factory and a `SyncBuilder` for you and starts the sync manager during `build()`:\n\n```typescript\nconst module = await new ReactorBuilder()\n  .withDocumentModelSources([/* ... */])\n  .withChannelScheme(ChannelScheme.CONNECT)\n  .buildModule();\n\nconst sync = module.syncModule?.syncManager; // ISyncManager | undefined\n```\n\n`withSync` is the full-control path: you hand over a pre-configured `SyncBuilder` when you need a custom channel factory, custom storages, or different limits. On this path the reactor builder still calls `syncManager.startup()` for you.\n\nThe gotcha is what happens when you call both. There is no error and no warning: **only the scheme path runs, and your custom `SyncBuilder` is discarded.** The scheme path always constructs a fresh `SyncBuilder` around the scheme's own factory, so any `withChannelFactory`, `withMaxInboxBatchSize`, or storage override you configured is silently thrown away. Use one or the other, never both.\n\nA second, related trap: `SyncBuilder.build()` and `buildModule()` do *not* call `startup()`. That call is only made for you when the builder is routed through `ReactorBuilder`. If you construct a `SyncBuilder` directly, you must call `syncManager.startup()` yourself before adding remotes, or `add` will operate on a manager that was never started.\n\nNote also that `withJwtHandler` only flows through the `CONNECT` factory; on the `SWITCHBOARD` path it is accepted and ignored.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/04-Synchronization.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:01.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:01.000Z"
    }
  },
